I thought of this while reading the Medusa thread and considering a
blindfolded Medusa. Q: How would she get blindfolded?  A: you
possessed her from the next room, made her put on a cursed blindfold,
then unpossessed her.

So: possession is a spell. When you cast it, you are asked to pick a
target monster; if it succeeds (monster fails saving throw) then you
begin controlling the monster chosen for d6*XL turns. While you
possess the monster, your original body is left behind, helpless;
other nearby monsters can attack it, and you will take damage and
possession will end on the next turn.

While you are possessing the monster, you can make it do anything it
could normally do: move around, pick things up, attack other monsters,
use potions or wands or scrolls (if it would be able to), jump into a
pit or other self-injurious behaviors, etc.

OK, this is WAAY too powerful, but it's just too fun to not think
about it. :-)


